## Database Setup

### SQL Server (Default)

```bash
# Install SQL Server (Linux)
sudo apt-get install mssql-server
sudo systemctl start mssql-server

# Connect to SQL Server
sqlcmd -S localhost -U sa -P YourPassword123
```

### PostgreSQL

Install the PostgreSQL provider:

```bash
dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Npgsql
```

Update `Program.cs`:

```csharp
// Replace UseSqlServer with UseNpgsql
options.UseNpgsql(connectionString);
```

Update `appsettings.json`:

```json
{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "Default": "Host=localhost;Database=<%= projectName || 'AspNetCoreApp' %>;Username=postgres;Password=postgres"
  }
}
```

### SQLite

Install the SQLite provider:

```bash
dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite
```

Update `Program.cs`:

```csharp
// Replace UseSqlServer with UseSqlite
options.UseSqlite(connectionString);
```

Update `appsettings.json`:

```json
{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "Default": "Data Source=<%= projectName || 'AspNetCoreApp' %>.db"
  }
}
```

### MySQL

Install the MySQL provider:

```bash
dotnet add package Pomelo.EntityFrameworkCore.MySql
```

Update `Program.cs`:

```csharp
// Replace UseSqlServer with UseMySql
options.UseMySql(connectionString, ServerVersion.AutoDetect(connectionString));
```

Update `appsettings.json`:

```json
{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "Default": "Server=localhost;Database=<%= projectName || 'AspNetCoreApp' %>;User Id=root;Password=password"
  }
}
```

## Running Migrations

### Using EF Core CLI

```bash
# Install EF Core CLI tools
dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef

# Create a new migration
dotnet ef migrations add CreateExamplesTable

# Apply migrations
dotnet ef database update

# Remove the last migration
dotnet ef database update LastGoodMigration

# List migrations
dotnet ef migrations list

# Remove a migration
dotnet ef migrations remove
```

### Using Package Manager Console

```powershell
# Create a new migration
Add-Migration CreateExamplesTable

# Apply migrations
Update-Database

# Remove the last migration
Update-Database LastGoodMigration
```

## API Endpoints

The following API endpoints are available:

### Root
- `GET /` - Application information
- `GET /health` - Health check

### API v1
- `GET /api/v1/examples` - List all examples (with pagination)
- `GET /api/v1/examples/health` - Health check
- `POST /api/v1/examples` - Create a new example
- `GET /api/v1/examples/{id}` - Get a specific example
- `PUT /api/v1/examples/{id}` - Update an example
- `DELETE /api/v1/examples/{id}` - Delete an example
- `PATCH /api/v1/examples/{id}/toggle-active` - Toggle example active status
- `POST /api/v1/examples/token` - Generate a JWT token (for testing)

### API Documentation
- `GET /api/docs` - Interactive Swagger UI
- `GET /api/docs/swagger.json` - Swagger JSON specification

## Adding Endpoints

1. Create a new controller class in the `Controllers` folder
2. Add the `[ApiController]` and `[Route]` attributes
3. Add endpoint methods with HTTP method attributes

Example controller:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;

namespace <%= projectName || 'AspNetCoreApp' %>.Controllers;

[ApiController]
[Route("api/v1/[controller]")]
public class NewController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpGet]
    public IActionResult Get()
    {
        return Ok(new { Message = "Hello from new controller!" });
    }

    [HttpGet("{id}")]
    public IActionResult GetById(int id)
    {
        return Ok(new { Id = id, Message = "Hello from new controller!" });
    }
}
```

## Adding Models

1. Create a new model class in the `Models` folder
2. Add the model to the `AppDbContext`
3. Create and apply a migration

Example model:

```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace <%= projectName || 'AspNetCoreApp' %>.Models;

public class NewModel
{
    [Key]
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [Required]
    [MaxLength(255)]
    public string Name { get; set; } = null!;

    public string? Description { get; set; }

    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; } = DateTime.UtcNow;
}
```

Update `AppDbContext.cs`:

```csharp
public DbSet<NewModel> NewModels { get; set; } = null!;
```

## Authentication

### JWT Bearer Authentication

The application includes JWT Bearer authentication. To use it:

1. Generate a token using the `/api/v1/examples/token` endpoint
2. Include the token in the `Authorization` header:

```
Authorization: Bearer your-token-here
```

### Configure Authentication in Controllers

```csharp
// Require authentication
[Authorize]
public class SecureController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpGet]
    public IActionResult Get()
    {
        return Ok(new { Message = "This is a secure endpoint" });
    }
}

// Require specific role
[Authorize(Roles = "Admin")]
public class AdminController : ControllerBase
{
    [HttpGet]
    public IActionResult Get()
    {
        return Ok(new { Message = "This is an admin endpoint" });
    }
}

// Allow anonymous access
[AllowAnonymous]
[HttpGet("public")]
public IActionResult GetPublic()
{
    return Ok(new { Message = "This is a public endpoint" });
}
```

## Authorization Policies

Create custom authorization policies in `Program.cs`:

```csharp
// Add a custom policy
builder.Services.AddAuthorization(options =>
{
    options.AddPolicy("RequireAdmin", policy =>
        policy.RequireRole("Admin"));

    options.AddPolicy("RequireEmailVerified", policy =>
        policy.RequireClaim(ClaimTypes.Email, "verified"));
});

// Use the policy
[Authorize(Policy = "RequireAdmin")]
public class AdminController : ControllerBase
{
    // ...
}
```

