## Deployment Options

### Azure App Service

```bash
# Publish the application
dotnet publish -c Release -o ./publish

# Deploy to Azure (using Azure CLI)
az webapp up --name <app-name> --resource-group <resource-group> --sku F1
```

### Azure Container Instances

```bash
# Build and push to Azure Container Registry
az acr build --registry <registry-name> --image aspnetcore-app:latest .

# Deploy to Azure Container Instances
az container create --resource-group <resource-group> --name <container-name> --image <registry-name>.azurecr.io/aspnetcore-app:latest --cpu 1 --memory 1 --ports 8080 --ip-address Public
```

### AWS Elastic Beanstalk

```bash
# Install AWS CLI and EB CLI
pip install awsebcli

# Initialize EB
eb init -p dotnet-core-8.0 aspnetcore-app --region us-west-2

# Create environment and deploy
eb create aspnetcore-env
```

### Google Cloud Run

```bash
# Build and push to Google Container Registry
gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/aspnetcore-app

# Deploy to Cloud Run
gcloud run deploy aspnetcore-app \
  --image gcr.io/YOUR_PROJECT_ID/aspnetcore-app \
  --platform managed \
  --region us-central1 \
  --allow-unauthenticated \
  --port 8080
```

### Railway

```bash
# Install Railway CLI
npm install -g @railway/cli

# Deploy
railway init
railway add postgres
railway up
```

### Render

1. Create a new Web Service on Render
2. Connect your GitHub repository
3. Set the build command: `dotnet publish -c Release -o ./publish`
4. Set the start command: `dotnet ./publish/<%= projectName || 'AspNetCoreApp' %>.dll`

### Fly.io

```bash
# Install Fly.io CLI
curl -L https://fly.io/install.sh | sh

# Deploy
flyctl launch
flyctl deploy
```

## Docker Configuration

### Dockerfile

The Dockerfile uses a multi-stage build:

1. **Build stage**: Uses the .NET SDK to restore dependencies and publish the application
2. **Runtime stage**: Uses the ASP.NET runtime image to run the published application

### Docker Compose

The docker-compose.yml sets up:

1. **web**: The ASP.NET Core application
2. **sqlserver**: SQL Server 2022 for database
3. **redis**: Redis for caching

